[**
 * Generates the profile-dependency Sankey diagram: its Mermaid
 * data file and the RST page embedding it.
 */]
[module profileDependencySankeyDocFile('http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/Types', 'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML', 'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML/Profile/Standard')/]

[import ucmism2t::queries::elementQuery/]
[import ucmism2t::queries::sankeyQuery/]
[import ucmism2t::templates::target::doc::rstUtilityDoc/]

[comment encoding = UTF-8 /]

[**
Generates the Mermaid Sankey data file (sankey.mmd) showing, for
each profile, how many dependency-supplier classes, data types, and
enumerations come from each source specification (package) -- e.g.
Schema, SKOS, CDIF itself. Left-hand nodes are specifications;
right-hand nodes are profiles; link values are combined item
counts.

Rows are sorted by specification name first, then by profile name,
so that all links from a given specification group together in the
generated source, matching the diagram's left-to-right reading
order. Rows with a zero count are never emitted -- Mermaid's sankey
diagram requires a strictly positive value on every link, and would
reject or misrender a zero-count row.

Written alongside the RST page that embeds it (same directory),
since the page's ".. mermaid:: sankey.mmd" reference is relative.

@param aModel - The UML model to generate the diagram data for.
/]
[template public generateProfileDependencySankey(aModel : uml::Model)]
  [file (aModel.u_filePath('doc').concat('/Appendices/ExploratoryDiagrams/sankey.mmd'), overwrite, 'UTF-8')]
    sankey
    %% Base Specifications (Left) -> [aModel.u_modelAcronym()/] Profiles (Right), Item Count
    %% source,target,value
    [for (aSpecificationName : String | aModel.u_allProfileDependencySpecificationNames())]
      [for (aProfilePackage : uml::Package | aModel.u_allProfilePackages())]
        [let aCount : Integer = aSpecificationName.u_itemCountForSpecificationAndProfile(aProfilePackage)]
          [if (aCount > 0)]
            [aSpecificationName/],[aProfilePackage.name/],[aCount/]
          [/if]
        [/let]
      [/for]
    [/for]
  [/file]
[/template]

[**
Generates the RST page embedding the profile-dependency Sankey
diagram, listed in the ExploratoryDiagrams toctree right after
InheritanceTreeVegaDiagram.rst. Mirrors
inheritanceTreeVegaDiagramDocFile.mtl's own structure (generation
message, anchor label, rst_header title), with an explaining
paragraph between the title and the diagram itself.

@param aModel - The UML model to generate the page for.
/]
[template public profileDependencyArchitecture(aModel : uml::Model)]
  [file (aModel.u_filePath('doc').concat('/Appendices/ExploratoryDiagrams/ProfileDependencyArchitecture.rst'), overwrite, 'UTF-8')]
    [aModel.rst_generationMessageDoc()/]
    
    .. _profileDependencyArchitecture:
    
    ['Profile Composition'.rst_header('=')/]
    
    This Sankey diagram illustrates the architectural alignment between the underlying metadata specifications (on the left) and
    the functional [aModel.u_modelAcronym()/] [aModel.u_modelMajorVersion()/].[aModel.u_modelMinorVersion()/] profiles
    that implement them (on the right).The thickness of the flowing bands directly corresponds to the volume of
    the distinct items borrowed from the base standards, visually emphasizing which specifications serve as
    the primary structural pillars for each profile.
    
    .. mermaid:: sankey.mmd
       :name: sankey
       :zoom:
       
    .. title is ignored
    .. :title: Structural Composition of [aModel.u_modelAcronym()/] [aModel.u_modelMajorVersion()/].[aModel.u_modelMinorVersion()/] Profiles
    .. only in sphinxcontrib.mermaid v2.x
    .. :mermaid_fullscreen:
  [/file]
[/template]
